{% aside type="danger" %}
**Always back up first.** Before any update, make full backups of your database and all FOSSBilling files. If something goes wrong, you'll need these to restore your data.
{% /aside %}

{% aside type="caution" %}
**Review version-specific notes.** Even patch releases can include breaking changes to themes, templates, APIs, and configuration. Read the upgrade guide for your target version **before** updating, especially if you use custom themes or modules.
{% /aside %}

## Automatic Updates (Recommended)

For most installations, the built-in updater is the easiest option:

{% steps %}
1. Log in to your admin panel
2. Go to **System → Update**
3. Click to install the update
{% /steps %}

FOSSBilling downloads and installs the new files, enables maintenance mode, clears the cache, and logs you out. After logging back in, you will be prompted to finalize the update.

### Update Finalization

Starting with 0.8.1, updates follow a two-phase process:

1. **Install** — New files are downloaded and deployed. Maintenance mode is enabled and you are logged out.
2. **Finalize** — After logging back in, FOSSBilling shows a finalization page where you apply any pending database patches. Once patches are complete, maintenance mode is restored to its previous state and you return to the dashboard.

This prevents older versions from automatically applying database patches before the new code is in place.

If you cannot access the admin panel after installing the new files, run the patcher from your FOSSBilling installation directory. Run it as the same system user that runs FOSSBilling’s web PHP process, with a PHP CLI binary that matches the site’s PHP version.

```bash
php console.php system:run-patcher
```

The updater follows the configured update branch, usually `release` or `preview`, which you can change in your [configuration file](/admin-guide/config/).

## Manual Updates

If you prefer to manage files yourself:

{% steps %}
1. **Back up your database and files**
2. [Download the latest release](https://fossbilling.org/downloads/stable)
3. Extract the files over your existing installation (overwrite existing files)
4. Delete the `install` folder that came with the new files
5. Log in to the admin panel and [finalize the update](#update-finalization)
{% /steps %}

If an update fails or FOSSBilling errors after updating, see [Troubleshooting FOSSBilling Issues](/maintenance/troubleshooting/#errors-after-updating).

## Docker Updates

The [Docker installation examples](/getting-started/docker/) store FOSSBilling in a named volume mounted at `/var/www/html`. A replacement container mounts that same volume over the application files bundled in the new image.

Pull a newer image and recreate the container to refresh PHP and Apache. Use the [built-in updater](#automatic-updates-recommended) to update FOSSBilling in the volume, then [finalize the update](#update-finalization) when prompted.

